<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#congreve-rocket">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congreve rocket</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Congreve rockets</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congreve rocket was a British military rocket developed by William Congreve in the early nineteenth century, based on rockets used in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>. It was inaccurate but had a strong psychological effect. A British-led coalition used Congreve rockets to defeat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>'s army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-katamansu">Battle of Katamansu</a> in 1826.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congreve-rocket.jpg" alt="Congreve rocket" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richie Bendall · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Congreve_in_1807.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
